// D&D's Levitate can target a willing ally (float them gently) or an
// unwilling creature (Constitution save, effectively a hard pin). No
// vertical-lift/anti-gravity `BuffEffect` exists at all (checked the full
// list in `common/src/comp/buff.rs` -- `MovementSpeed`, `GroundFriction`,
// `SwimSpeed` and friends only ever scale horizontal movement or ground
// friction, nothing addresses vertical position), so the "gently float a
// willing ally" branch has no delivery mechanism whatsoever and is dropped.
// Kept branch: the unwilling/hostile CC framing, modeled with
// `BuffKind::Rooted` ("Reduces movement speed to 0") as "suspended
// helplessly, unable to proceed" -- the same primitive this batch's
// `earthbind.ron`/`earthen_grasp.ron` already use for their own closest-CC
// fit, matching the sheet's own 18m range and single-target shape exactly
// (unlike a touch-ally melee redirect, which would contradict the sheet's
// real 18m reach).
BasicRanged(
    energy_cost: 30,
    buildup_duration: 0.35,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 0,
            buff: Some((
                kind: Rooted,
                dur_secs: 10.0,
                strength: Value(1.5),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            damage_kind: Bludgeoning,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 55.0,
    num_projectiles: Value(1),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Transmutation),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
